# Phaser game code

Side-view 2.5D, not a platformer and not top-down. Along-pitch position and depth (near to far sideline) are separate from sprite jump height. Sort sprites by depth. The camera follows the ball along a pitch wider than the screen.

```ts
new Phaser.Game({
  type: Phaser.AUTO,
  width: 384,
  height: 216,
  pixelArt: true,
  roundPixels: true,
  physics: { default: "arcade" },
  scale: { mode: Phaser.Scale.FIT, autoCenter: Phaser.Scale.CENTER_BOTH },
});
```

- Scenes: boot, menu, match. Match rules live in the match scene, not in the menu.
- Teams and players: one typed module. Names come from `.cursor/skills/starman-soccer/references/roster.md`.
- English UI strings: one module. No scattered literals for labels the player reads.
- Arcade physics is for motion. Do not add a physics engine, a backend, or another rendering library.
- Do not smooth pixel art (`pixelArt: true`, no linear filter on sprites).
